    <!-- Help sheets (plain-language explanations behind the "?" buttons) -->
    <string name="help_ndvi_title">What is crop health (NDVI)?</string>
    <string name="help_ndvi_body">Satellites measure how green your maize is. Green, strong maize gives a high number. Weak or dry maize gives a low number.\n\nWe compare your plot with what is normal for maize planted on the same day. If your plot stays below normal for more than one satellite pass, we tell you.</string>
    <string name="help_confidence_title">What does confidence mean?</string>
    <string name="help_confidence_body">Confidence shows how sure the system is. Clouds and missing pictures lower it.\n\nWhen confidence is low, a person checks the result. A plot is never judged on missing data.</string>
    <string name="help_coverage_title">What is insurance cover?</string>
    <string name="help_coverage_body">A covered plot is insured for the season. If satellites see a big loss, a claim starts by itself.\n\nYour cooperative or insurer adds plots to the cover. You do not pay in the app.</string>
    <string name="help_forecast_title">How is the harvest forecast made?</string>
    <string name="help_forecast_body">We add up how green your maize has been this season and compare it with past seasons on the same plot.\n\nIt is an early prototype and a wide range. It is not a promise about your harvest.</string>
    <string name="help_claims_title">How do claims work?</string>
    <string name="help_claims_body">1. Satellites watch every covered plot.\n2. If the loss passes the agreed level, a claim starts by itself. You do not need to fill a form.\n3. An insurance officer checks the evidence. An agent may visit.\n4. If approved, the payout goes to your mobile money (simulated here).\n\nYou can ask for a review once for each decision.</string>
    <string name="help_how_it_works_title">How Rinda works</string>
    <string name="help_how_it_works_body">1. Add your maize plot by drawing it on the map.\n2. Your cooperative agent checks the plot.\n3. Satellites look at your maize every 5 days.\n4. If your maize looks weak, you get an alert.\n5. If a covered plot loses too much, a claim starts by itself and a person decides it.</string>
    <string name="help_planting_title">Why does the planting date matter?</string>
    <string name="help_planting_body">Maize grows differently each week. We compare your plot with normal maize of the same age, so the planting date must be right.\n\nYour cooperative agent can correct it.</string>
    <string name="help_draw_title">How to draw your field</string>
    <string name="help_draw_body">1. Move the map to your field. Pinch with two fingers to zoom.\n2. Tap each corner of the field, one after another, going around the edge.\n3. Tap at least 3 corners. The green shape shows your field.\n4. Made a mistake? Tap Undo, or Start again.</string>

